  "chapter": {
    "number": 6,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "For the End, a Psalm of David among the Hymns for the eighth."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, rebuke me not in your wrath, neither chasten me in your anger.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Pity me, O Lord; for I am weak: heal me, O Lord; for my bones are vexed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My soul also is grievously vexed: but you, O Lord, how long?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Return, O Lord, deliver my soul: save me for your mercy's sake.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For in death no man remembers you: and who will give you thanks in Hades?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 11
          },
          {
            "text": "I am wearied with my groaning; I shall wash my bed every night; I shall water my couch with tears.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My eye is troubled because of my wrath; I am worn out because of all my enemies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Depart from me, all you⌃ that work iniquity; for the Lord has heard the voice of my weeping.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord has listened to my petition; the Lord has accepted my prayer.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let all my enemies be put to shame and sore troubled: let them be turned back and grievously put to shame speedily.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 11,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. I have laboured.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 6,
          "verse": 6
        }
      }
    ]
